  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Friday)\nIssued at 1215 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nWarm and dry weather conditions will persist across the Mid-South\nthis week as an anomalous ridge maintains its grip over the\ncentral CONUS. Geopotential heights at 500 mb are at the max of \nclimatology across the Upper Midwest and still well above the 90th\npercentile as far south as the Lower MS Valley. While this ridge \nwill become less amplified throughout the week, 500 mb heights \nwill remain well above climatology across the Southeast, \nmaintaining the status quo. Column precipitable water will remain \nin the vicinity of 0.50\" through most of the week, which is \nroughly half of the climatological norm for late October. \nEfficient diurnal mixing will promote generally low relative \nhumidity values each afternoon and wider-than-normal diurnal \ntemperature ranges. Keeping with the recent theme, no \nprecipitation is expected through the work week.\n\nPersistent troughing over the western CONUS will result in\nsouthwesterly flow aloft from the Southern Plains into the Middle\nMS Valley by midweek. Individual shortwave troughs will pass far\nto the north of the CWA, but we should see some impact via\nincreased mid/high clouds from day to day. The stubborn surface\nanticyclone over the OH Valley will gradually shift farther east\nthis week, but proximity to this high will limit southerly wind\nspeeds and the subsequent moisture return.\n\nThere may be some light at the end of the tunnel, or rather a\nfaint glow of light. A strong subtropical jet is projected to\nround the base of the western trough and propagate across the\nSouthern Plains. This may be just enough of a nudge to the east\nto advect some deeper moisture into the region over the weekend.\nEnsemble guidance is hinting at increasing rain (liquid that\nfalls from the sky) chances by Saturday. Confidence is low in the\ntiming, as these split flow patterns upstream of a blocking ridge\noften arrive later than initially suggested by numerical guidance.",
